Official PETSA commit: 87853d888e98311ac94e64be920d17b57143b20c

The official adapters compute and print per-window adapted MSE/MAE arrays but do
not save them. The main program subsequently runs Predictor on a mutated model
without the adapter calibration path and labels those results "without TSF-TTA".
This instrumentation-only patch saves the already computed adapter arrays. It
does not change model inputs, predictions, losses, optimizer steps, or metrics.

Files: tta/petsa.py and tta/tafas.py

  import os
  ...
  os.makedirs(self.cfg.RESULT_DIR, exist_ok=True)
  np.save(os.path.join(self.cfg.RESULT_DIR, "adapt_test_mse_all.npy"), self.mse_all)
  np.save(os.path.join(self.cfg.RESULT_DIR, "adapt_test_mae_all.npy"), self.mae_all)

File: predictor.py

The predictor already retains both per-window arrays, but returned and saved
only MSE.  Add `mae_all` to the return dictionary and save it as
`test_mae_all.npy`.  This is likewise observation-only and is needed for paired
MAE tests against the adapted arrays.

Execution compatibility note (no source edit): TEST.BATCH_SIZE is set to 4096
so the official cursor loop receives the full 3389-window ETTh1 test dataset in
one outer DataLoader batch. With the default 256, batch_start is not reset across
outer batches and the official assertion fails after processing only one batch.
